# ─── TLS Certificate files — NEVER commit to git ─────────────────────────────
#
# Private keys and certificates contain sensitive cryptographic material.
# Committing them would expose the private key to anyone with repo access,
# permanently compromising the TLS security of asc.premoscorp.com.
#
# How to get certificates:
#   Dev/staging:  bash scripts/gen_selfsigned_cert.sh
#   Production:   Let's Encrypt — see docs/TLS_SETUP.md
#
# Files expected here (never committed):
#   fullchain.pem  — certificate chain (cert + intermediates)
#   privkey.pem    — private key (KEEP SECRET)
#   dhparam.pem    — DH parameters (optional, for DHE ciphers)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.csr
*.p12
*.pfx
*.der
